### Brief: key ( database key )
# Effects that pick where a courtier or guest goes when they leave a court and enter the pool.
# Only two keys are used by code, both required:
#	destination_for_courtier_entering_pool - used for characters who have an employer (courtiers)
#	destination_for_guest_entering_pool - used for characters without an employer (guests)
# Any other key is loaded but never used.
#
# The entry body is an effect block. It's run just before on_courtier_ready_to_move_to_pool / on_guest_ready_to_move_to_pool fire.
# The province saved as scope:destination is then passed as scope:destination to that on_action.
# If scope:destination isn't set, the destination is empty.
#
# Only interface effects are allowed (such as save_scope_as). Other effects log an error and are skipped.
# The random seed is fixed, so random effects always give the same result.
#
# Supported scopes:
#	root: none
#	scope:mover ( character ) - the character leaving the court
#
key = {
	scope:mover = {
		...
		host.capital_province = { save_scope_as = destination }
	}
}
